  "description": "Each auto trigger (ADR-0010), read in the order model-asked, cases, changes-existing, and only where the run proposed something: declared cases exist (the pack's saved tests), the proposal changes an existing pack, or the model called request_review. The trigger that held is the reason and the trigger; with none, the critic does not run and the reason is the layer that set auto. Each item is the decision for the case beside it in cases (by position): session, the session's critic members (tool-offer.json: critic, criticProject, criticReasoning, adversarialReview); table, the policy table's (budget.json: criticDefault, criticReasoningFloor, adversarialReview); forced, the forced-off facts (child, phase, purpose, reviewerAssigned); run, the run's facts where the critic would start (proposal, cases, changesExisting, modelAsked, room); author, the author's tier on the run's capability (absent: none stated). Written by hand; criticSwitch.test.ts and go/context/critic_test.go compute each decision and hold it equal.",
